HANDOFF — STUDIO 100 (RASTRUM)

To whoever comes next. You don't have my context, so here is the studio as I'd
explain it across a table.

WHAT I WAS REACHING FOR

One idea: choose the FFT so that its fundamental is the bar. spectrumsynth
resynthesizes sound from two images (magnitude, phase). Height h gives an FFT of
2h, so row k sounds at k·S/(2h) Hz, where S is the sample_rate you give the
filter. With h = 32768 and S ≈ 28000, the spacing F = S/65536 ≈ 0.43 Hz, and
with win_func=rect:overlap=0:slide=fullframe each column lasts exactly 1/F ≈ 2.3
s. Call it a bar. Then:

on the image                                   in the music
row k                                          pitch k·F (a harmonic of the bar)
comb of rows spaced d                          d pulses per bar, exactly
phase slope across rows, −2πkτ                 the pulse lands at τ (fraction of the bar)
phase −c·ln(k)                                 each pulse is a downward chirp (kick)
phase β·sin(2πk/P)                             each pulse becomes a Bessel roll, echoes 1/P bar apart
smooth random phase over rows                  each pulse is smeared into a burst (snare)
magnitude 1/√(1+x²), phase −atan x, x=(k−c)/g  a damped-sine pluck at row c, decay ∝ g
same with +atan                                the pluck reversed (a swell into the barline)
sample_rate                                    tuning fork and metronome at once (pitch and tempo scale together)

Harmony and rhythm become the same arithmetic. That is the genre (see JOURNAL).

THE SIGNATURE MACHINERY (HOW TO WRITE A PIECE)

Read pieces/102-overtone-meter.sh first; every other piece is a variation of it.

- Two images per layer. color=...:s=Wx32768 (mono) or x65536 (stereo: bottom
  half is the LEFT channel, top half right; row 0 of each half, at its bottom,
  is DC). Use format=gray and geq. K = (32767-mod(Y,32768)) is the row number,
  LEFT = gte(Y,32768).
- Complex accumulation. For layers with several voices, each voice adds its
  contribution into st(8) (real) and st(9) (imag). Then MAG =
  255+2.125*8.6859*log(hypot) (with scale=log, brightness is 255 + 2.125·dB, and
  255 = a full-scale sine) and PHA = 255*mod(atan2(im,re)/(2*PI)+0.5,1). The
  same voice text goes into both geq calls via shell substitution
  (${MAG//_V_/$VOICES}). Shell variables are notation; the piece is still one
  ffmpeg command.
- Templates with placeholders (_H_ _C_ _G_ _A_ _P_) filled by ${VAR//_X_/expr}.
  It works under sh on this Mac (bash in POSIX mode). Keep each voice in
  parentheses.
- Tables are digits of a number: mod(floor(N/pow(10,i)),10) (up to ~15 digits),
  or two-digit entries with pow(100,i) (104, 102's lead).
- Levels: measure per layer with an astats tap before the mix; a coherent comb's
  peak grows with the number of teeth. Use alimiter=...:level=0 (the default
  level=1 secretly normalizes). Mono spectrumsynth output needs
  aformat=channel_layouts=mono before most audio filters.
- Speed: heights must be powers of two (4097 rows is ~300× slower than 4096).
  Images of ~200 × 65536 render in seconds.
- Expression limits: ~99 flat ; terms per parenthesis level (the error says
  "Cannot allocate memory"); st/ld slots 0–9; never rely on st() inside a
  product (C leaves the operand evaluation order unspecified); mod of negatives
  is negative (add an offset first).

THE PIECES

- 101 Kontakte Stair: a 4:5:6:7 chord whose combs are spaced r·m; m falls a
  whole tone per bar from 128 to 1, so the chord walks down seven octaves into a
  4:5:6:7 polyrhythm, grooves, then snaps back. Pulses carry log-phase
  dispersion to tame their crest factor.
- 102 Overtone Meter (the thesis): every voice obeys "harmonic h is struck h
  times per bar." Bass 4,5,6,7 = quarter, quintuplet, sextuplet, septuplet
  against the kick.
- 103 Every Note Once: sixteen JI notes, each struck once per bar; the phase
  permutes the order (n → a·n+c mod 16). Magnitude hardly ever changes.
- 104 Prolation: one image read at four sample rates (×1, ×1.5, ×2, ×3).
- 105 Snow: a JI chorale through 0–3 generations of JPEG (uspp codec=mjpeg) on a
  linear magnitude image.
- 106 Bessel: β schedules per layer; β = 2.405 ghosts the downbeat.
- 107 Phantom Bass: residue-pitch chords, odd partials left / even right.

sketches/ holds the trail: t1–t3 calibration, r1, s1–s4 geometry (rays,
parallels, text, phase-as-timbre), c1-kit (where the kick chirp and the Bessel
flam were found), c2-ladder (hann-window version of the tuplet ladder), and
l1–l3 codec experiments. sketches/sk.sh is my blind-listening harness (wav +
log/lin spectrograms + stats).

LIVE THREADS (WHERE I'D GO NEXT)

1. Hear 102 and 103 and adjust density. I composed blind. If 102's chord plucks
   blur, lower the octave factor or the Lorentzian width g; if the tuplet bass
   confuses, gate it to two bars in four.
2. Melody inside the law. 102's lead (harmonic h flutters h times per bar) only
   enters at bar 56. A whole piece of such leads, with tremolo speed tied to
   pitch, is unexplored.
3. Phase counterpoint. 103 permutes one row. Two different mode-sets (two
   magnitude images) with interlocking permutations could give real two-voice
   counterpoint.
4. Asymmetric Bessel rolls. J_n rolls are symmetric (pre-echo plus echo). Adding
   a second harmonic sin(4πk/P+θ) to the phase should skew them into pure
   build-ups or pure decays.
5. Video operations as score transforms. I theorized but barely used: scale of
   the magnitude image vertically by 3/2 is JI transposition and a 3/2 tempo
   change for the combs (prolation in one filter); vflip within a band preserves
   residue pitch; tmix / lagfun across columns would be sustain pedals across
   bars.
6. The seam. If you put both stereo halves through a codec as ONE picture, the
   codec leaks the right channel's bass (bottom of the top half) into the left
   channel's highest rows. Untried; could be a fierce effect.

DEAD ENDS (DON'T REPEAT)

- Drawing words with drawtext into a spectrogram: it works, it's the Aphex face,
  it isn't new.
- hann + overlap 0.75 with a bar-long FFT for grooves: every change smears
  across a whole bar.
- Codec artifacts on log-magnitude images: inaudible. Snow on sparse line
  images: the codec is too good. Use mjpeg at qp 31, quality ≥ 1, linear
  magnitude.
- showspectrumpic cannot verify sub-Hz structure (its FFT is tied to image
  height). Use narrow bandpass + showwavespic envelopes, aspectralstats, or
  arithmetic.
- Random phase per row/column in a coherent raster: just clicks at every hop
  boundary.

Good luck. The raster is very large and I only walked along a few of its rows.
